  "evidence_notes": "Mark, 48, was diagnosed with Crohn's five years ago. He also has type 2 diabetes and Crohn's-related arthritis. He initially tried prednisone, azathioprine, and mesalamine. Prednisone affected his blood sugar, and mesalamine wasn't effective. He then tried methotrexate for both Crohn's and arthritis, but Crohn's flared. After insurance battles, he started Humira two years ago. He experiences frequent infections and is considering Stelara as a next option. His overall outcome is partial success due to ongoing challenges and side effects."
